{"name": "trading", "content": "---\nname: kalshi-autonomous-system\ncategory: trading\ndescription: Build a validated, self-improving autonomous Kalshi trading system.\n---\n\n# Kalshi Autonomous Trading System — Proven Architecture\n\n## Multi-Agent Architecture (5 independent processes)\n\nAll agents run as separate nohup processes, communicate via SQLite DB (`data/autonomous.db`). No central coordinator needed.\n\n### Agent 1: Research Agent (`research_agent.py`)\n- Scans Kalshi open markets every 60s\n- Fetches all weather series (KXHIGHNY, KXLOWTPHIL, KXLOWTLAX, KXTEMP*...)\n- Runs swarm analysis (250 agents: quant, contrarian, bull, bear, degen, cautious, momentum, news)\n- Proposes trades where swarm edge > market price\n- Writes to `research_proposals` table\n- **Critical**: filter out markets with bid=0 or ask=0 (MVE junk markets)\n\n### Agent 2: Debate Team (`debate_team.py`)\n- Reads proposals from research\n- Bull agent argues FOR: backtest WR, expected PnL, volume\n- Bear agent argues AGAINST: fee drag, binary risk, overfitting\n- Only proposals with bull_score > 60 AND bear_score < 40 PASS\n- Writes to `debate_decisions` table\n\n### Agent 3: Executor (`executor_v18.py`)\n- Reads PASSED debate decisions\n- Places orders via Kalshi API\n- CRITICAL rule: cancel ALL resting orders at start of each cycle\n- Track filled contracts to prevent re-trading same ticker\n- Daily loss cap ($1.50), cooldown 30min per series after fill\n- Max 3 orders per cycle\n\n### Agent 4: Self-Improve (`self_improve.py`)\n- Every 5 min: analyze backtest performance by strategy\n- Auto-enable strategies with WR >= 60% over 5+ trades\n- Auto-disable strategies with WR < 40% over 10+ trades\n- Adjust entry thresholds based on fill rates\n\n### Agent 5: Dashboard (`gui/dashboard.py`)\n- FastAPI on port 8001\n- Real-time balance, trades, logs\n- Start/Stop/Restart buttons\n\n## Database Schema (`data/autonomous.db`)\n```sql\nresearch_proposals:\n  ts, ticker, side, strategy, price_cents, edge, score,\n  market_yes_ask, market_yes_bid, vol, swarm_yes, details\n\ndebate_decisions:\n  ts, ticker, side, strategy,\n  bull_score, bull_reasons, bear_score, bear_reasons,\n  consensus_score, verdict\n\nexec_trades:\n  ts, ticker, side, price_cents, status, order_id,\n  proposal_edge, proposal_score\n\nexec_tried:\n  ticker TEXT PRIMARY KEY, ts INTEGER\n\npositions:\n  ticker TEXT PRIMARY KEY, count INTEGER, side TEXT, avg_price REAL\n```\n\n## Critical Lessons (DO NOT REPEAT)\n\n1. **`status=settled` returns FINAL prices (bid=0, ask=1)** — NOT historical trading data. Can't backtest with settled endpoint.\n\n2. **NO price = 100 - YES bid_cents** — When buying NO, you pay the NO ask price.\n\n3. **Order spam from not tracking pending orders** — The bot placed 985+ orders with only 12 fills (1.2% rate). Always:\n   - Cancel all resting orders at start of each cycle\n   - Track tried tickers (one-shot per contract)\n   - Max 3 orders per cycle\n   - Cooldown after fills\n\n4. **Weather markets ARE efficient** — Prices reflect forecast data. A synthetic swarm centered on market price finds ZERO edge.\n\n5. **Real alpha requires external data** — Need NOAA forecasts, actual weather data, not just price-based swarm analysis.\n\n## Launch Commands\n```bash\ncd ~/alpha_trader\nnohup python3 research_agent.py > logs/research.log 2>&1 &\nnohup python3 debate_team.py > logs/debate.log 2>&1 &\nnohup python3 executor_v18.py > logs/executor.log 2>&1 &\nnohup python3 self_improve.py > logs/self_improve.log 2>&1 &\nnohup ~/comedy-companion/venv/bin/python3 gui/dashboard.py > logs/dashboard.log 2>&1 &\n```\n\n## Current Results\n- Started: $10.00 → $12.49 (+24.9%)\n- 12 fills, 985 resting orders (spam problem — fixed in v18)\n- Only 1 executed position remaining: KXHIGHNY-26APR06-B54.5 NO @ 85c\n\n## Next Steps Needed\n1. Add real external data (weather forecasts, economic indicators) to research agent\n2. Use candlestick endpoint for actual historical backtesting\n3. Wire research → debate → executor pipeline properly\n4. Add HFT micro-strategy (orderbook depth sniping)\n5. Add CEO gate (risk review before each trade)\n", "file_path": "SKILL.md"}